# Architecture & Code

## Stack
Next.js App Router · TypeScript · Tailwind · static-first · Vercel.  
MDX for long-form when migrating; current Markdown/`_posts` is fine until content migration.  
Future Supabase OK — do not overbuild early.

## Structure (target; migrate gradually)
- `app/(content)/`, `app/(tools)/` — thin route files
- `components/{layout,content,ui,tools}/`
- `lib/{content,seo,utils}/`
- `content/{posts,hubs,cities}/`
Keep: content layer · UI · tools · data helpers · SEO metadata separated.

## Coding
- TypeScript everywhere; Server Components by default; Client only for interaction
- Small single-purpose components; explicit props; avoid files ≫250 lines
- No god components; no business logic dumped in `page.tsx`
- Reuse before inventing; extract repeated UI (CTA, FAQ, callouts, disclosures)

## Next.js / SEO
- `generateMetadata` on indexable pages; unique title + description
- Prefer static generation; semantic HTML; heading hierarchy; internal links
- Centralize SEO helpers in `lib/seo` when adding more pages — no duplicated metadata logic

## UI
**Tropical Paradise** (mandatory) — [`tropical-paradise.md`](tropical-paradise.md), tokens in `globals.css`.  
Sunny cream surfaces, Ocean Teal CTAs, coral/mango accents, pill buttons, `TropicalCard` patterns.  
Avoid: dark themes, Scandinavian sage/`rounded-sm`, Terracotta clay, purple/glow SaaS, crowded OTA dashboards, loud affiliate blocks.  
Mobile-first; clear primary vs outline CTA hierarchy; lively but soft transitions (`hover:scale-105` with reduced-motion).

## Forbidden
Generic placeholder copy · mixing article render + app logic · random fonts/styles that ignore site system · overengineering unvalidated features.

## Before / after changes
Before: classify request (content / tool / SEO / UI); check existing components; respect IA.  
After: types, imports, route placement, mobile layout, metadata impact, brand tone.
